<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Swedish–Novgorodian Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th–14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Swedish–Novgorodian Wars were a series of conflicts between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and the Novgorod Republic over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karelia">Karelia</a> and the trade routes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-finland">Gulf of Finland</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neva-river">Neva</a>. Swedish expeditions and the building of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vyborg">Vyborg</a> in 1293 and Landskrona in 1300 met Novgorodian counter-attacks. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-noteborg">Treaty of Nöteborg</a> of 1323 set the first border between them, though fighting continued intermittently.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/swedish-novgorodian-wars.jpg" alt="Swedish–Novgorodian Wars" width="320" height="302" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cattette · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eastern_expansion_of_Sweden.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
